{"key":"gaming-sets","items":[{"name":"Dice set","key":"srd_dice-set","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_dice-set/"},{"name":"Playing card set","key":"srd_playing-card-set","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_playing-card-set/"}],"name":"Gaming set","desc":"This item encompasses a wide range of game pieces, including dice and decks of cards (for games such as Three-­‐‑Dragon Ante). A few common examples appear on the Tools table, but other kinds of gaming sets exist. If you are proficient with a gaming set, you can add your proficiency bonus to ability checks you make to play a game with that set. Each type of gaming set requires a separate proficiency.","document":"srd-2014","crossreferences":{"to":[]}}
{"key":"heavy-armor","items":[{"name":"Chain mail","key":"srd_chain-mail","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_chain-mail/"},{"name":"Plate Armor","key":"srd_plate-armor","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_plate-armor/"},{"name":"Ring mail","key":"srd_ring-mail","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_ring-mail/"},{"name":"Splint Armor","key":"srd_splint-armor","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_splint-armor/"}],"name":"Heavy Armor","desc":"Of all the armor categories, heavy armor offers the best protection. These suits of armor cover the entire body and are designed to stop a wide range of attacks. Only proficient warriors can manage their weight and bulk.\r\n\r\nHeavy armor doesn't let you add your Dexterity modifier to your Armor Class, but it also doesn't penalize you if your Dexterity modifier is negative.","document":"srd-2014","crossreferences":{"to":[]}}
{"key":"holy-symbols","items":[{"name":"Amulet","key":"srd_amulet","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_amulet/"},{"name":"Emblem","key":"srd_emblem","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_emblem/"},{"name":"Reliquary","key":"srd_reliquary","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_reliquary/"}],"name":"Holy Symbols","desc":"A holy symbol is a representation of a god or pantheon. It might be an amulet depicting a symbol representing a deity, the same symbol carefully engraved or inlaid as an emblem on a shield, or a tiny box holding a fragment of a sacred relic. Appendix PH-­‐‑B \"Fantasy-­‐‑Historical Pantheons\" lists the symbols commonly associated with many gods in the multiverse. A cleric or paladin can use a holy symbol as a spellcasting focus. To use the symbol in this way, the caster must hold it in hand, wear it visibly, or bear it on a shield.","document":"srd-2014","crossreferences":{"to":[]}}
{"key":"light-armor","items":[{"name":"Leather Armor","key":"srd_leather-armor","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_leather-armor/"},{"name":"Padded Armor","key":"srd_padded-armor","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_padded-armor/"},{"name":"Studded Leather Armor","key":"srd_studded-leather-armor","url":"https://api.open5e.com/v2/items/srd_studded-leather-armor/"}],"name":"Light Armor","desc":"Made from supple and thin materials, light armor favors agile adventurers since it offers some protection without sacrificing mobility. If you wear light armor, you add your Dexterity modifier to the base number from your armor type to determine your Armor Class.","document":"srd-2014","crossreferences":{"to":[]}}
